---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Callout from "@dst/ui/Callout.astro";
---
<Layout
  title="Coffee in Azizi Riviera"
  description="Where to get coffee in Azizi Riviera — what's actually on the promenade, and how coverage varies building to building."
>
  <section class="container hero">
    <p class="eyebrow">Coffee</p>
    <h1>Coffee on the promenade</h1>
    <p class="lede">
      The ground-floor promenade is where this actually happens — cafes are
      one of the earliest tenant types to fill in as each stretch of
      buildings opens, alongside casual dining and convenience retail.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="container">
    <h2>What to expect</h2>
    <p>
      A mix of independent cafes and small chain outlets along the
      canal-facing promenade, walkable from most buildings without a car.
      Coverage isn't uniform — the longer-established stretch of the
      promenade has more open than the newer phases — so what's actually
      running changes as the development continues to fill in.
    </p>
  </section>

  <Callout kind="warn">
    This page describes what's typically available, not a fixed list of
    named cafes — the promenade's tenant mix changes as Riviera continues
    to build out. Confirm a specific spot is open before making it the
    reason for a visit.
  </Callout>
</Layout>

<style>
  .hero { padding-top: var(--space-5); }
  .lede { font-size: var(--step-1); color: var(--ink-muted); max-width: 65ch; }
</style>
